body:
I've been trying to use a macro with the leader key Following the directions, I have this

```
behaviors {

    leader: leader { 
       compatible = "zmk,behavior-leader-key"; 
       #binding-cells = <0>; 
       de_ae { sequence = <A E>; bindings = <&my_macro>; };
    }; 
}

```

where `my_macro` is defined above in the macros section. However, 
I get this error during compilation:

`ERROR: /behaviors/leader POST_KERNEL 219 < /macros/my_macro POST_KERNEL 220`

I suspect that I might not be able to put a macro 
in the bindings for leader because everything works fine if I do 
this instead,


```
behaviors {

    leader: leader { 
       compatible = "zmk,behavior-leader-key"; 
       #binding-cells = <0>; 
       de_ae { sequence = <A E>; bindings = <&kp X>; };
    }; 
}
```

Any ideas?
